 "notes": "Chart 3 of 16. Ledger grid on the right page (p.107); the four printed annotations are on the left page (p.106). yearHeader \"1938\" prints just above the DATE label.\n\nChecksums (KP = US + BS) verified on every row where all three are present: 45 3/8+48 1/4=93 5/8; 46 1/2+49 7/8=96 3/8; 48 1/2+50 7/8=99 3/8; 51 1/4+53 1/4=104 1/2; 53 3/4+55 1/8=108 7/8; 54 7/8+58 1/8=113; 56 7/8+60 1/8=117; 58 3/8+61 5/8=120; 60 7/8+62 1/2=123 3/8; 55 5/8+56 3/4=112 3/8. On rows where BS is blank (JULY1, 7, 12, 25) KP still equals US + last recorded BS. These checksums also confirmed several fraction reads, notably BS \"49 7/8\" on the 21st (46 1/2+49 7/8=96 3/8, ruling out 49 1/8).\n\nInk convention holds throughout: Upward Trend = black, Downward Trend = red, and Secondary Rally / Natural Rally / Natural Reaction = blue (pencil).\n\nTwo distinct underline systems: (1) HEADER carried-forward pivots are underlined in BLACK \u2014 38 single, 40 double, 78 double (Downward Trend reds); 49 single, 52 double, 101 single (Natural Rally blues); 39 3/4 single. (2) IN-CHART pivotal points carry short, drawn, number-width RED single underlines marking up-leg tops (BS 62 1/2 on 7/2, US 61 3/4 & KP 124 1/4 on 7/7, BS 63 1/8 on 7/19, US 63 1/4 & KP 126 3/8 on 7/25) and natural-reaction lows (BS 56 3/4 on 7/11, US 55 1/2 & KP 112 1/4 on 7/12). These red marks are clearly distinct from the printed thin blue/red full-width grid rules.\n\nAnomaly flagged in headerEntries: the natural-reaction trio checksums to 79 (US 39 1/4 + BS 39 3/4 = KP 79), and US (39 1/4) and KP (79) sit in the Natural Reaction column in blue, but BS's 39 3/4 is written in RED directly below 40 in the Downward Trend column. Transcribed as DT because both x-position and ink agree; noted because the checksum shows it functions as the Bethlehem natural-reaction value.",
